MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_001: Oh, what am I to do? It's fair to say this is the most\nimportant decision of my life, and yet...
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_002: Dietrich. He's a mighty specimen to be sure,\nbut is he...the one?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_003: Could I be the one for him? Even I am no match for\nhis beauty or his noble rank from a far-off land.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_004: Not to mention the strength that felled Cetus,\nthe Sea Tyrant. Who could ever be found worthy?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_005: Then again, there are quite a few rumors about him\nbeing a crazed killer. That could be a problem.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_006: And suppose he's the type to just up and leave.\nEnough. I should just arrange a meeting.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_007: I do not understand your hesitation. I am\nalways ready.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_008: Eek! Dietrich?! How long have you been\nstanding there?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_009: Since you spoke of beauty.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_010: So then you also heard the part about you being a\ncrazed killer and that being a problem?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_011: Because it wouldn't really be a problem for ME, \nof course. It was just a rumor I heard about town.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_012: {SetColor=Gray}Am I going to be killed for this? Oh, please let him\nbe in a good mood.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_013: You look fearful. Rumors are merely rumors.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_014: Of course! I know that, of course! I wasn't scared\nin the slightest!
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_015: Then duel me. That is the surest way to determine\nthe truth.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_016: Duel? Hold on. I'm not sure I follow your train\nof thought...
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_017: Yet you desire a duel, do you not? Why else would\nyou study me? So have it! If you fall, I am your killer.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_018: No, no! I think there has been a misunderstanding.\nI have no desire to do any of that.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_019: So you lack the will. I had heard you are a knight,\nbut you shrink from a challenge.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_020: Excuse me? You may be a great warrior, Dietrich,\nbut I cannot let your insult stand.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_021: I shrink from nothing. But this is no place or occasion\nfor a knight to battle. Another time, perhaps.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_022: Oh! Good. I look forward to it.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_023: Oh my, that was close... I thought I was done for.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_C_024: What am I going to do? I had no idea the most\nimportant decision of my life would be so...perilous.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_001: What a hopeless establishment. They put up an\nimpressive facade, but their wares are mere garbage.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_002: Catania! I crave our duel. How long must I wait?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_003: Dietrich! Hello! Um, I mean...
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_004: If, as you suggested, this is no place for a knight to\nfight, then when will we face off?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_005: Hm? Is it not obvious? I will only risk my life where\nand when a lord worthy of my service commands it.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_006: I fight under the order of my lord, not the order of\nmy heart or feelings.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_007: Hmm.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_008: Unfortunately, I have yet to find that lord. The one\nwho would be worthy of my life and service.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_009: I see. I long for this battle, but you will not fight until\nso ordered.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_010: Indeed. I relish any opportunity to show off my\nconsiderable skills and offer a victory to my lord.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_011: Such restraint must be taxing on you. I oft thirst for\nblood, and so often fight.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_012: So I've heard. You were bound for the Isle of Eif. The\nGáe Bolg Colosseum is home to many great fighters.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_013: Oh, so you know? You are well-informed.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_014: Any warrior or knight of worth is aware of its\nreputation. Wait. Could this be...a real conversation?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_015: What of it?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_016: {SetColor=Gray}With just a little backstory, I'm suddenly cozying up\nto the crazed killer. Well done, Catania.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_017: {SetColor=Gray}Not to say he's not scary. He is. But he's also a\ngood listener. What a catch!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_018: I can't hear you.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_019: What? Oh, um... Sorry, I was talking to—\nabout myself. Right?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_020: You are difficult to understand. Do you mean to say\nthere is to be no duel?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_021: Then I will wait for you to be ready. I will in fact...\nwait forever.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_022: You'll wait for me...forever?
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_023: Heehee! I'm flattered. I honestly had no idea you'd\nbe so interested.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_024: Perhaps I can't duel you at the moment, but I could\njoin you for dinner.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_025: We wouldn't even have to talk about battles. We\ncould discuss our interests, get to know each other...
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_026: That sounds very dull. I think not.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_027: Wh-what?! But we've been getting along so well.
MID_SE_Dit_Cat_B_028: What about tea then? I'd be honored to have your\ncompany. Hey! Where are you going?